  "judge_reasoning": "# Evaluation Analysis\n\n## Task Requirements\nThe task was to solve the differential equation y''(t) - 2y'(t) + 10y(t) = 0 and display its general solution.\n\n## Screenshot Analysis\n\n**Screenshot 1:** Shows the WolframAlpha homepage with an empty search input field.\n\n**Screenshot 2:** Shows the differential equation \"y''(t) - 2y'(t) + 10y(t) = 0\" correctly entered into the WolframAlpha search box.\n\n**Screenshot 3:** Shows the page in a loading state after submitting the query.\n\n**Screenshot 4 & 5:** Show the results page with:\n- **Input:** y''(t) - 2y'(t) + 10y(t) = 0\n- **ODE classification:** second-order linear ordinary differential equation\n- **Differential equation solution:** y(t) = c₁ e^t sin(3 t) + c₂ e^t cos(3 t)\n- Sample solution family plots and plots of sample individual solutions\n\n## Verification of Mathematical Correctness\n\nThe characteristic equation is r² - 2r + 10 = 0, giving roots r = (2 ± √(4-40))/2 = 1 ± 3i. The general solution is therefore y(t) = e^t(c₁ cos(3t) + c₂ sin(3t)), which matches exactly what WolframAlpha displayed and what the Result Response states.\n\n## Response vs. Screenshot Consistency\n\nThe Result Response states: \"y(t) = c_1 e^t sin(3 t) + c_2 e^t cos(3 t)\" — this matches the solution displayed in the screenshots exactly.\n\n## Conclusion\n\nBoth parts of the task were completed:\n1. ✅ The differential equation was solved (via WolframAlpha)\n2. ✅ The general solution is displayed on screen: y(t) = c₁ e^t sin(3t) + c₂ e^t cos(3t)\n\nThe solution shown is mathematically correct and consistent between the screenshots and the response.\n\n## Verdict: **SUCCESS**",
